            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The local application of strong opioids seems to offer relief for the patient suffering from eschars, tumorous wounds or ulcers thanks to peripheral opioid receptors. Morphine mixed with a hydrogel is the most commonly used method.</AbstractText>
